__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.coverage

mutants/

# hypothesis example database, written beside the tests on every
# local run of the property modules; scratch, never the record.
.hypothesis/

# Backslash-named scratch files a Windows-simulated test run leaves
# in the tree on a POSIX host; never the record, and git on Windows
# cannot check them out.
\\tmp\\*

# Agent and deployment state -- the agent's papers. An agent's
# approval memory (the saved record of what its operator approved
# and need not be asked again), a deployment's config, and the
# runner's state files are private-shelf material: they stay on
# the operator's disk, out of every commit. The patterns live
# here, in the project, so the protection clones with the tree
# instead of depending on one machine's global excludes -- the
# arrangement that failed publicly in November 2026, when a
# coding agent's local approval file reached public repositories
# in over a thousand secret-bearing copies (the research is
# summarised in docs/steady/security/privacy-design.md).
# .claude/settings.json is shareable project settings by design
# and is deliberately not ignored; it must never hold a secret.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/config.json
seen.json
board.json
oracle-chat.jsonl
oracle-briefs.jsonl
outbox/
work/
